# Projects

Purpose:
  Project registry. Contains example/template project instances
  and is the parent directory for real project instances.

  IMPORTANT: .sdd/projects/ is NOT permanently empty.
  It contains:
    - example_project/ — example/template project for demonstration
    - {project_name}/   — real project instances created after human selection

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @example_project/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [PRJ1] example_project/ is a template, not a real project.
  [PRJ2] Real project instances are created at .sdd/projects/{project_name}/.
  [PRJ3] Project instances are created AFTER human selects a project name.
  [PRJ4] Before project selection, only example_project/ exists.
  [PRJ5] Migration commands run against real project instances.
  [PRJ6] The project/ folder contains reusable schemas only.

Lifecycle:
  1. Human provides project name (e.g. "my-app")
  2. AI creates .sdd/projects/my-app/ from example_project/ template
  3. AI populates my-app/ with project-specific data
  4. All work proceeds in .sdd/projects/my-app/
  5. example_project/ remains as reference/template

Navigation:
  ProjectModel: @../project/INDEX.sdd
  ExampleProject: @example_project/INDEX.sdd
  Migration: @../commands/sdd-migrate.sdd
  Features: @../features/INDEX.sdd

State: +
